The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of Lithuania (the Constitution of 25 October 1992 as amended,
the laws amending it, and Constitutional Court documents), as published by the Register of Legal Acts
(Teisės aktų registras, www.e-tar.lt), read through Internet Archive captures, and checked against the Seimas's
own copy of the Constitution (www.lrs.lt), retrieved 29 October 2026. Legal acts are not objects of copyright
under art. 5 of the Law on Copyright and Related Rights of the Republic of Lithuania (Lietuvos Respublikos autorių
teisių ir gretutinių teisių įstatymas).

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph or point per
line; typesetting was normalised (spaces, double quotes to „…“, a spaced hyphen to an en dash); the Register's notes
under articles and its change lists were left out; for 1996-2006, each amending law's own words were applied to the
text before it; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the acts that made each change. The
wording of the law was not changed. Neither the Register of Legal Acts nor the Seimas endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
